    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nDepends on: https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/35101\n\nJumping to URLs is a common action inside terminal buffers. Once URL retrieval is supported, maybe we could have default mappings to jump to the next / previous URL? Or at least a simple API to achieve that?\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nInside a terminal buffer: \n- `]u` jumps to the next URL\n- `[u` jumps to previous URL\n\nWe don't have to use these mappings, specifically. [`vim-unimpaired`](https://github.com/tpope/vim-unimpaired) already uses `[u` / `]u`, in what I believe to be a non-conflicting way (they cannot be used inside a terminal buffer).\n\nOf course, not a priority in any way :)",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
