        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> mappings to jump to the next / previous URL? Or at least a simple API to achieve that?\n\nErgonomic API: yes. presumably these are just extmarks, right? If iterating extmarks isn't ergonomic already, then we should drive towards that. What's missing from `nvim_buf_get_extmarks()` ?\n\nI've long wanted to unify \"legacy marks\" and \"extmarks\" from a user perspective, and https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40743 indicates that the UI can work.\n\nSo a similar step could be to think about how the existing `]'` and `['` could work with extmarks. But most likely a \"fuzzy picker\" makes more sense for extmarks because there tend to be a lot of them.",
